.TH USB-GIT 1 "July 2026" "gway-001" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usb-git \- bastion-gated GitHub CLI wrapper for gway-001
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-git
[\fB--operator\fR \fINAME\fR] \fIgh-arguments\fR...
.br
.B usb-git
\fBbootstrap\fR [\fB--token-file\fR \fIPATH\fR | \fB--from-gh-auth\fR]
.br
.B usb-git
\fBinstall-hooks\fR [\fIREPO\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usb-git
wraps the GitHub CLI on gway-001. Normal read-only GitHub operations pass
through to
.BR gh .
Privileged operations such as repository administration, pull-request merges,
release writes, secrets, variables, mutating
.B gh api
calls, and protected direct git pushes require the verified bastion USB key.
.P
The wrapper logs start and finish events to the local operator interaction log
and installs pre-push hooks that protect main, tags, deleted refs, and
non-fast-forward updates.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B bootstrap
Encrypt a GitHub admin token for bastion-gated use and install the main push
guard hooks in the default local Arthexis checkouts.
.TP
.B bootstrap --from-gh-auth
Use the currently authenticated GitHub CLI token as the token source.
.TP
.B bootstrap --token-file PATH
Use a token read from
.IR PATH .
The token is encrypted locally; it is not printed.
.TP
.B install-hooks
Install the pre-push guard in the supplied repositories. With no repositories,
the default local Arthexis checkouts are used.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/usb-git/admin-token.enc
Bastion-key-encrypted admin token.
.TP
.I ~/.config/usb-git/main-guard.marker.enc
Bastion-key-encrypted marker used by the git push guard.
.TP
.I ~/.local/lib/usb-git/pre-push-main-guard.sh
Protected push hook target.
.TP
.I ~/logs/usb-interactions.log
Local interaction log.
.SH SAFETY
.B usb-git
does not gate ordinary local repository inspection or read-only GitHub queries.
It gates publication and destructive repository actions behind the verified
bastion USB key.
